{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43279 - PROTEIN:5787",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- and RXF 631 through a series of target interactions involving the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol, Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate, and 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol. All these compounds share a common pathway of interaction with the proteasome regulatory subunit, which ultimately leads to a target of RXF 631. The evidence suggests that Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- may act through a similar mechanism, possibly by modulating the proteasome regulatory subunit, thereby influencing RXF 631's activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- in modulating the proteasome-dependent pathways that are targeted by RXF 631.",
